<title>JAPAN: Oresundskonsortiet launches 5.27% yen/dlr samurai.</title>
<headline>Oresundskonsortiet launches 5.27% yen/dlr samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual-currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead manager Kokusai Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Oresundskonsortiet</p>
<p> GUARANTORS	Denmark and Sweden</p>
<p> AMT		 10 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.27 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  25 April 2000</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  25 April 1997</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	April 17 to April 24</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Kokusai Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Sumitomo Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: The exchange rate was fixed at $3,938.55 per 500,000 yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
